- op: discuss  # b893
  at: '2026-06-07T06:43:58Z'  # b893
  by: agent  # b893
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b893
  clock: 2  # b893
  nonce: b893  # b893
  message: "Dogfood finding (member F154.A2, independent), reproduces on the frozen substrate. Mechanism: the field name not_captured is reused with disjoint semantics in two different top-level blocks. limits.not_captured lists source constructs the analysis did not parse (dynamic imports, eval, monkey-patching, complex decorators); reproducibility_context.not_captured lists reproducibility factors not pinned (transitive deps, OS/libc, hardware). Same key name, two unrelated meanings, in two blocks. Scope: 2 top-level blocks (limits, reproducibility_context) each carry a not_captured array with non-overlapping semantics; affects every run output. Exposure/consequence: a consumer that searches the behavior map for not_captured (or writes generic handling keyed on the field name) conflates \"constructs not analyzed\" with \"reproducibility factors not pinned,\" producing a confused completeness assessment. Expectation: a field name denotes one concept across the document; two distinct concepts get two distinct names. Distinct from WI-togop (limits.not_captured is a hardcoded universal constant) and from INV-lifik symptom (3) (which is the edge.meta-vs-node.meta field-name collision, not this top-level-block collision). Cross-ref WI-togop, INV-lifik."  # b893
- op: discuss  # b413
  at: '2026-06-07T10:03:23Z'  # b413
  by: agent  # b413
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b413
  clock: 3  # b413
  nonce: b413  # b413
  message: "Dogfood re-confirmation. Two unrelated top-level blocks both define a hardcoded constant named not_captured with disjoint referent semantics: _REPRO_NOT_CAPTURED at schema.py:201 (3 environmental factors: transitive package versions; OS/kernel/libc/locale/timezone; hardware/floating-point) under reproducibility_context.not_captured (spec §744), vs KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.copy() at limits.py:173 (6 construct categories: dynamic imports, eval/exec, ...) under limits.not_captured (spec §955). Both are documented; both are hardcoded module constants. A consumer reading 'not_captured' without tracking the parent block conflates 'we did not record the OS version' with 'we do not analyze eval()' — a category error about what the analysis missed."  # b413
